WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.376 --> 00:00:03.552
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:05.096
- [Jurgen] People enjoy mayhem,

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:07.434
especially when it
happens to other people.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:10.301
There's definitely a
factor of schadenfreude

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:13.176
in watching something go terribly wrong

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:14.509
to someone else.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.339
- [Narrator] You're in a U-Haul.

00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:27.880
You're about to start your
first semester at Duke,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.949
and driving down the
road you see this sign.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:30.965
And another sign.

00:00:30.965 --> 00:00:32.287
You pay no attention,

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:34.371
and then this sign lights up,

00:00:34.371 --> 00:00:36.204
and then disaster strikes.

00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:38.604
You're about to get
your 15 minutes of fame

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.421
all thanks to this man.

00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:41.766
- [Jurgen] Hi, I'm Jurgen Henn.

00:00:41.766 --> 00:00:43.491
- [Narrator] And he's
infamous in these parts.

00:00:43.491 --> 00:00:44.494
Right, Jurgen?

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:46.430
- One can say that yes, I am,

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.593
known as the 11 foot
8 guy around here.

00:00:49.593 --> 00:00:51.669
- [Narrator] Jurgen and his
wife started 11foot8.com,

00:00:51.669 --> 00:00:53.673
which is what exactly?

00:00:53.673 --> 00:00:57.185
- 11 Foot 8 website records
all the truck crashes

00:00:57.185 --> 00:01:00.132
that happen here at the
11 foot 8 bridge.

00:01:00.132 --> 00:01:04.952
It's really all it is. (laughs)

00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:09.593
Eight years ago I set up a
camera outside my office here,

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:11.673
and started recording the traffic

00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:15.150
that goes under the
railroad trestle behind me.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.683
Within a few weeks, I recorded

00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:21.993
a truck crashing into the railroad bridge.

00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:23.399
- [Narrator] Since installing the camera,

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:26.484
Jurgen has uploaded video of
113 crashes at the bridge,

00:01:26.484 --> 00:01:29.044
and amassed over 10 million views.

00:01:29.044 --> 00:01:31.583
Most bridges in the state
have a 15 foot clearance.

00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:32.986
The 11 foot 8 bridge, however,

00:01:32.986 --> 00:01:36.153
was built 100 years ago,
hence the lower height.

00:01:36.153 --> 00:01:37.423
And now thanks to Jurgen,

00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:40.702
these crashes have a dedicated following.

00:01:40.702 --> 00:01:44.021
- Our fans are really intensely
interested in these crashes,

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:45.882
and they love to buy souvenirs,

00:01:45.882 --> 00:01:47.624
little piece of crash art.

00:01:47.624 --> 00:01:49.200
- [Narrator] Uh, what's crash art?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.367
- The crash art are bent,
mangled pieces of aluminum

00:01:54.274 --> 00:01:57.978
that usually form the frame of the truck.

00:01:57.978 --> 00:02:01.364
And the impact crushes that aluminum

00:02:01.364 --> 00:02:04.498
and kind of twists it
in interesting shapes.

00:02:04.498 --> 00:02:07.263
People will buy the
crash art, they love it.

00:02:07.263 --> 00:02:08.804
For some of them it's almost like

00:02:08.804 --> 00:02:11.298
owning a piece of the Berlin Wall.

00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:13.023
- [Narrator] Why doesn't the
town just raise the trestle

00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:14.442
or lower the road?

00:02:14.442 --> 00:02:15.444
- [Jurgen] From the perspective

00:02:15.444 --> 00:02:17.583
of the city and the state DOT,

00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:20.303
the low clearance is clearly marked,

00:02:20.303 --> 00:02:24.437
and it's up to the driver
to decide their next move.

00:02:24.437 --> 00:02:26.342
Structural changes at this intersection

00:02:26.342 --> 00:02:28.383
would be extremely costly.

00:02:28.383 --> 00:02:29.844
- [Narrator] Well at least
we have these awesome videos.

00:02:29.844 --> 00:02:30.781
Right?

00:02:30.781 --> 00:02:33.443
- I get no satisfaction
out of seeing a new crash.

00:02:33.443 --> 00:02:37.322
If we found an actual solution
to prevent this tomorrow,

00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:39.822
I'd be all over it, I love it.

